{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1010718-2e-mots","id":1010718,"title":"[2E] Mots","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-01T11:18:49-08:00","id":1010718,"title":"[2E] Mots","content":"Mots are specially Germanic and Scandinavian groups from <b>Blasphemies</b> book. In 1E they were special local variants of Lodges, but I\u2019m wonder if they should still be in 2E? Even then, how could they work in 2E <b>Werewolf</b>?<br /> Examples from <b>Blasphemies</b> are:<ul><li><i>Valkyries</i> \u2013 Sisterhood of Uratha that send their most greatest of warriors to Vallhalla. I\u2019m thinking maybe of \u2018great warrior\u2019 or simply \u2018died in battle\u2019 as Sacred Prey of Lodge here.</li> <li><i>Eiwaz</i> \u2013 Racist group saying that being werewolf makes you greater than any mortal. I\u2019m thinking about making them Pure Lodge splint off from <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/867500-apocalypse-tribes-as-2e-lodges?p=867680#post867680\">Get of Fenris</a>, for Ivory Claws and Predator Kings. Even then, I have no idea on the Sacred Prey of them.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T13:09:43-08:00","id":1010783,"title":"","content":"They're just lodges linked thematically. And with culture or tradition. The Pillars are effectively mots of the tribes.","signature":"","edi